<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Falcon half year shr, gold output falls.</title>
<headline>Falcon half year shr, gold output falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (US cts)  4	     vs 12</p>
<p>    Div (US cts)	    10	    vs 15</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   0.12	  vs 0.34</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.04	  vs 0.72</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.13 credit vs 0.07 charge</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.06	  vs 0.09</p>
<p>    Turnover		  14.45	 vs 14.61</p>
<p>Full name: Falcon Investments SA</p>
<p>NOTE - The company, which is the ultimate holding company of Falcon Gold Zimbabwe Ltd, said gold production was 39,784 ounces compared to 42,530 oz in the six months to March 31, 1996. The decrease was mainly due to reduced yield at the Dalny Mine complex.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
